{
  "dom_id": "step-2228",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Identifying an Integral Expression For the Area of a Petal of a General Polar Curve",
  "problem": "Which of the following represents the area enclosed by the first petal of the polar curve  $r = 1+\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\left(2\\theta+\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),$ represented by the shaded region shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226023/assets/95138031d082cfc739c2c2569af9a9ea5c63d4b6990237b8267c4b2fe2481b09.png)",
  "worked_solution": "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} r^2(\\theta) \\: \\textrm{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r(\\theta) = 1+\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\left(2\\theta+\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{(1+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the integration limits. \n\nThe curve bounding the region crosses itself at the origin. Therefore, we want to find the values of $\\theta$ for which $r=0$, or \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta +\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, the first petal extends from the third quadrant to the first quadrant. Since the petal begins in the third quadrant, it is convenient to allow negative values of $\\theta$ when determining the interval.\n\nThe solutions for $2\\theta+\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ closest to $0$ on either side are\n\n$$\n2\\theta+\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = -\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}, \\dfrac{3\\pi}{4} \n\\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad \n2\\theta = -\\dfrac{5\\pi}{4}, \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n\\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad \n\\theta = -\\dfrac{5\\pi}{8}, \\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the first petal is traversed for \n\n$$\n\\theta  \\in \\left[-\\dfrac{5\\pi}{8}, \\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right].\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that this interval lies between the first and fourth quadrants, the same as our petal.\n\nTherefore, our expression for the area is given by\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{1}{2}\\int_{-5\\pi/8}^{\\pi/8}  \\left( 1+\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\left(2\\theta+\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\\right)^2 \\: \\textrm{d}\\theta.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-2228\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"2228\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"636\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-2228\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-9\">Identifying an Integral Expression For the Area of a Petal of a General Polar Curve</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"2228\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            